Purpose: disable semaphore DOP gating and ensure every CS IDLEDLY < MAXCNT.
Source: Linux 7c53ff050ba88bb37eed3e17f2bb8ec592d83302
  "drm/xe: Apply Wa_16023105232".
Adaptation for 6.14: reuse existing RC_SEMA_IDLE_MSG_DISABLE bit 12 and RTP
  range/ENGINE_BASE helpers; retain upstream graphics/media ranges and VF
  skip. Initialize timestamp_base from RPM_CONFIG0 even in 6.14's divide-
  logic CTC branch, without changing reference-clock selection.
  Use 64-bit picoseconds and floor((MAXCNT_ps - 1) / IDLEDLY_unit_ps): the
  supplied upstream u32 multiplication can overflow and its corrective
  conversion mixes ns/ps. Clamp to the field, preserve reserved bits, clear
  INHIBIT_SWITCH_UNTIL_PREEMPTED. Warn/skip on zero MAXCNT or unknown clock
  rather than divide by zero or underflow. Register defaults normally comply.

